name: sim.setShapeTexture
description: Applies/removes a texture to/from a shape
luaSynopsis: sim.setShapeTexture(int shapeHandle, int textureId, int mappingMode, int options, list uvScaling, list position = None, list orientation = None)
pythonSynopsis: sim.setShapeTexture(int shapeHandle, int textureId, int mappingMode, int options, float[2] uvScaling, float[3] position = nil, float[3] orientation = nil)
inputs:
1. shapeHandle: handle of the shape.
2. textureId: ID of the texture or -1 to remove any existing texture. See also sim.getTextureId, sim.getShapeTextureId and sim.createTexture
3. mappingMode: texture mapping mode.
4. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0: if set (1), then adjacent texture pixels are not interpolated.
    - bit1: if set (2), then the texture is applied as a decal (its appearance won't be influenced by light conditions).
    - bit2: if set (4), then the texture will be repeated along the U direction.
    - bit3: if set (8), then the texture will be repeated along the V direction.
5. uvScaling: array of 2 values indicating the texture scaling factors along the U and V directions
6. position: array of 3 values x/y/z indicating the texture position on the shape. Can be None/nil for default values
7. orientation: array of 3 values (Euler angles) indicating the texture orientation on the shape. Can be None/nil for default values
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: texture:set, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_set.method
- name: texture:setData, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_setData.method
- name: texture.applyMode, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_applyMode.property
- name: texture.interpolate, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_interpolate.property
- name: texture.repeatU, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_repeatU.property
- name: texture.repeatV, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_repeatV.property
